 ### [NeRF Restarting Approach](12980-nerf-restarting-approach.md)
-The NeRF Restarting Approach is a training schedule for joint pose and radiance field optimization that eliminates artifacts learned during the pose refinement phase by discarding the neural network weights and retraining from scratch. Unlike staged training, which freezes poses and continues training the existing networks, this method re-initializes both coarse and fine Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs) after pose convergence. It is chosen when the initial joint optimization introduces persistent artifacts into the scene representation that persist even after pose stabilization. See [NeRF Restarting Approach](12980-nerf-restarting-approach.md).
